		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">30</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following are some hints for coming up with new test cases.

1. Normal test cases - length of the array is like 5, 8 and 10 .
1.1 When all the elements are different, there exist an integer P for which there are exactly P numbers greater than P in the array.
1.2 When all the elements are different, there is no integer P for which there are exactly P numbers greater than P  in the array.
1.3 When all the elements are same, there is no integer P for which there are exactly P numbers greater than P  in the array.
1.4 When all the elements are different, and there are more than 1 integer P for which there are exactly P numbers greater than P  in the array.

2. Boundary test cases
2.1 When all the elements are same, and still for an integer P there are exactly P numbers greater than P  in the array.


Based on these hints, you can come up with at least 5 new test cases.
Write them on a paper along with the expected output.</attribute>
